      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mac): allow slow node worker startup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCold macOS node-host worker startup can exceed the fixed 20-second deadline while loading config and plugin capabilities. The app then kills a healthy worker before it emits `ready`, so the Mac node never connects and none of its native computer-control capabilities appear on the Gateway.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nKeep the hard startup deadline, but raise the default to a generous two minutes. Make the bound injectable for deterministic tests and cover delayed readiness beyond the former production assumption.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSlower Mac node workers can finish cold discovery and connect normally. Truly hung workers still fail closed after a bounded startup window.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Reproduced on a five-Mac fleet: a healthy worker emitted `ready` after roughly 25 seconds and was killed at 20 seconds.\n- `swift test --package-path apps/macos --filter MacNodeHostWorkerTests` — 8 tests passed.\n- Signed macOS app build completed and passed `codesign --verify --deep --strict`.\n- Fresh structured autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
